      "narrative": "Pinal County’s residential market is currently stable to slightly rising in price, with its median single-family home price recently reported at $382,000, up 0.1% while the broader Greater Phoenix median rose 1%.[11] Inventory in Pinal County has expanded modestly, with months of supply increasing to 4.4 months, indicating a more balanced market and giving buyers somewhat more choice.[11] Closed and pending sales have slipped (closed sales down 0.5%, pending sales down 5.3%, new listings down 5.7%), suggesting softer transactional volume and slightly less urgency on the buy side even as prices hold.[11] Local dynamics continue to be influenced by Pinal’s role as a more affordable alternative to Maricopa County and by growth in cities like Maricopa and Apache Junction, where recent data show modest month-over-month price gains and relatively typical marketing times around 7-11 weeks.[12][14][2][6][7][9][10][15]",
